---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="Our privacy policy: cookieless analytics, no data resale, GDPR rights, and the sub-processors that operate this site.">
  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">Short version: we collect nothing that identifies you.</p>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Data we collect</h2>
      <p>
        This website (vhsgreed.win) does not require accounts, does not set
        functional cookies, and does not ask for personal information. We
        operate no newsletter and no comment system. We use a cookieless
        analytics service and a separate traffic-measurement service, both
        described below.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Google Analytics 4 (GA4):</strong> we use Google Analytics to
        understand how the site is used. It loads a tracking script and uses
        first-party cookies and local storage to measure page views and to
        group sessions. It reports aggregate statistics (pages, referrers,
        rough geography, device type) and identifies users only as anonymous
        numeric IDs, not by name or email. Google processes this data under
        its own privacy policy; see
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Google's privacy policy</a> and
        <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/7318509" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        how Google uses data from Google Analytics</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics:</strong> a cookieless analytics
        service that reports aggregate statistics (page views, referrers,
        device types, approximate geographic region). It does not use
        cookies, does not profile visitors, and cannot identify an
        individual.
      </p>
      <p>
        Both answer the same question, "is anyone reading this?" not "who
        is reading this?" We do not read individual session data or any
        personal identifier from either service.
      </p>

      <h2>Purchases</h2>
      <p>
        Payments are processed by Gumroad, which operates under its own
        privacy policy. We receive the delivery details you provide to
        Gumroad (such as an email address for download access) and nothing
        more. We do not store payment card data; we cannot see it.
      </p>

      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>
        If you email us, we keep the correspondence to answer it. We do not
        add you to any list.
      </p>

      <h2>Third parties</h2>
      <p>
        The site is served by Cloudflare (hosting, HTTPS, analytics).
        Google processes analytics data through Google Analytics 4. All
        other links (GitHub, Medium, Bluesky, Gumroad) are subject to their
        own policies.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Sub-processors:</strong> Cloudflare, Inc. (hosting, CDN,
        Web Analytics, DNS), Google LLC (Google Analytics 4), Gumroad, Inc.
        (payments and download delivery), and the respective operators of
        GitHub, Medium, and Bluesky where you interact with those services.
        No data is sold or shared beyond what is required to operate this
        site and deliver purchases.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under applicable law (including GDPR) you can request what data we
        hold about you; in practice, for this site, the answer is: none.
        Contact us via the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>
        for any privacy question.
      </p>
      <p class="muted"><small>Last updated: 2026-08-31.</small></p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>